@startuml
skinparam defaultFontSize 11
skinparam ArrowFontSize 10
skinparam state {
  FontSize 11
  AttributeFontSize 10
  BorderThickness 1.2
  BackgroundColor #FAFAFA
  BorderColor #333333
  BackgroundColor<<term>> #E8E8E8
  BorderColor<<term>> #555555
}

title GreenThread session FSM (post-migration, coarsened)

[*] --> Ready : new_session(task)

state Ready     : pending scheduler dispatch;\n has work remaining
state Running   : executing a quantum\n on a worker thread
state Suspended : parked awaiting an\n inter-session message
state Forked    : parent has just spawned\n child sessions (rare)
state Completed <<term>>
state Failed    <<term>>
Completed : terminal — normal form reached
Failed    : terminal — error or cost exhaustion

Ready     --> Running   : schedulerDispatch(worker)\n / startQuantum
Running   --> Running   : quantumEnd  [hasMoreWork]\n / enqueueSelf
Running   --> Suspended : blockOn(ChannelId::InterSession(c))\n / park(waiting_on = c)
Suspended --> Ready     : interSessionMsg(c)\n / unpark
Running   --> Completed : quantumEnd  [normalForm]\n / deliver(RhoOutcome)
Running   --> Failed    : evalError | costExhausted\n / record(error)
Running   --> Forked    : spawnChild(categories)\n / register(children)
Forked    --> Ready     : forkComplete\n / enqueueSelf

Completed --> [*]
Failed    --> [*]

note right of Forked
  **Session-level parallelism only.**
  Object-language <b>P | Q</b> goes directly to
  Rholang's <b>Par</b> constructor and is handled
  inside the DebruijnInterpreter — not via
  this FSM. (See §10.1–10.2.)
end note

note right of Suspended
  <b>waiting_on</b> lists inter-session
  <b>ChannelId::InterSession(_)</b> handles, not
  RSpace names. Intra-session blocking on a
  Rholang <i>consume</i> is handled inside the
  DI lifeline, not at this FSM layer. (§10.4)
end note

note right of Ready
  Transitions labelled
  <b>event [guard] / action</b>
  per Harel-style statechart semantics.
end note

@enduml
